 "notes": {
  "general": "Raw rates count process failures as task failures; clean_rate excludes them as a diagnostic. gpt-oss:20b's five ollama-500 serving deaths were resampled as full episodes and failed on the merits. qwen3:8b's level1<level2 residual is a model profile, not a content defect: its persistent level1 failures carry ~20% larger input contexts and 16 of 20 involve catalog-listing discovery - the discover driver dilutes a small model's context in the everything-mounted workspace, while its single-call policy execution at level2 is strong. Four of five models order level1 >= level2 after the extend rung swap and the listing-discipline fix. Pass is outcome-only: a process failure after every graded check has passed (trailing malformed turn, wrap-up timeout) no longer voids the episode; three such episodes were recovered (GLM-5.2 level1, gpt-oss:20b level2, qwen3:8b level2).",
